WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:05.705
Oh, we made it down to Chatham.

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:07.707
Oh, I hope we get a bite.

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:09.809
Staying positive.

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:12.112
You see, the whales,
the tuna are generally with them.

00:00:12.312 --> 00:00:13.646
We started to hear them.

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:16.116
We set up, basically down sea of them.

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:19.953
Tons of bait here that they're feeding on.

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:21.921
Hopefully the tuna come through this.

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:23.523
Just deployed our first two baits.

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:25.291
We'll see what happens.

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:27.961
We won this thing last year
by coming down to Chatham

00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:31.231
all the time,
but also by working with the hot tuna.

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:34.267
So we're going to continue with that
as long as possible

00:00:35.335 --> 00:00:37.170
Did you find the whales Bob?

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:40.540
yeah, we know they're upwind of us.

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.476
We can hear them. Okay.

00:00:43.476 --> 00:00:44.778
We're right close to Bobby's.

00:00:44.778 --> 00:00:47.047
Just right up the line
a little bit from us here.

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:48.481
Chris crying like a baby's here.

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:50.950
I can't get them walk or a bite.

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:53.253
And me and Bob Cook on the fat tuna.

00:00:53.253 --> 00:00:55.588
Stay in contact on the radio.
More efficient Chatham.

00:00:55.922 --> 00:00:58.291
Anyone that's willing to steam down here
and put in the time

00:00:58.291 --> 00:01:01.261
and the effort deserves
to be given the right information.

00:01:01.428 --> 00:01:03.163
I thought we'd be headed home by now.

00:01:04.364 --> 00:01:05.899
Of course we all did.

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:09.002
I heard a rumor that the hard merchant
fishing at Chatham, which to me is odd.

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:10.937
You know, he's
the one who's been hating on Chatham.

00:01:10.937 --> 00:01:12.939
He says he's going to stay local
in Gloucester.

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:15.942
I think it might be BS,
but it's too early in the season

00:01:15.942 --> 00:01:17.911
to stress about the other boats.

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:19.846
Usually when we're cooking, we hook up.

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:22.515
So hopefully it brings us a little luck
here.

00:01:22.515 --> 00:01:25.418
I’d love to bend the rod
and get in early enough

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:29.823
